        "text": "*[Bug 18341] aov() with constant data returns different p-values depending on sample size &amp; balancedness*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=18341>\n\n--- Comment #7 from Deepansh Khurana (<mailto:deepanshkhurana@outlook.com|deepanshkhurana@outlook.com>) ---\n(In reply to Benjamin Tyner from comment #6)\nI agree with your point of view here, Benjamin. We are adding two quantities\nthat maybe shouldn't be added. The same approach is in `lm.R` for a similar\nfunction, so we brought it over.\n\nFor context, the `lm.R` version:\n\n```\nif (is.finite(resvar) &amp;&amp;\n        resvar &lt; (mean(f)^2 + var(c(f))) * 1e-30)  # a few times\n.Machine$double.eps^2\n        warning(\"essentially perfect fit: summary may be unreliable\")\n```\n\nThe comment in `lm.R` suggests this codifies the same thing, but I like the\nmore explicit solution you shared.\n\nDo you suggest we resolve it in both `aov.R` and `lm.R` here, or we first close\nthis and then branch off into a new issue to fix this for both?",
