        "text": "*[Bug 18959] undoc(dir=) differs from undoc(package=)*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=18959>\n\n--- Comment #4 from Michael Chirico (<mailto:michaelchirico4@gmail.com|michaelchirico4@gmail.com>) ---\nOffering an LLM investigation which basically pinpoints the issue, but omitting\nthe proposed solution about which I'm more agnostic. It did find this comment\nin the code which is evocative:\n\n```\n&lt;NOTE&gt;\nThere is no point in worrying about exportClasses directives\nin a NAMESPACE file when working on a package source dir, as\nwe only source the assignments, and hence do not get any\nS4 classes or methods.\n&lt;\/NOTE&gt;\n```\n\n<https:\/\/github.com\/r-devel\/r-svn\/blob\/b5a50cb201993f64bd62d6c1d0b610e6f3dbef6e\/src\/library\/tools\/R\/QC.R#L229-L278>\n\nWhich means the QC.R code assumes that {diffobj} approach of assigning the\noutput of `setClass()` doesn't occur.\n\n---\n\nThe inconsistency between `undoc(dir=)` (checking source directory) and\n`undoc(package=)` (checking installed package) for S4 classes and methods was\ncaused by two main issues in how `undoc(dir=)` processed the source files:\n\n1.  **Incomplete Evaluation of S4 Definitions:**\n    To find objects in `dir` mode, R sources the package files into a temporary\nenvironment. However, it was using `.source_assignments` which only evaluated\ntop-level assignments (matching `&lt;-` or `=`).\n    *   S4 classes defined *with* assignment (e.g., `MyClass &lt;-\nsetClass(\"MyClass\", ...)`) were evaluated and registered.\n    *   S4 classes defined *without* assignment (e.g., `setClass(\"MyClass\",\n...)`) were ignored.\n    *   S4 methods (typically defined using `setMethod(...)` without\nassignment) and S4 generics defined without assignment were also ignored.\n\n2.  **Missing NAMESPACE Filtering for S4 Objects:**\n    While `undoc(dir=)` filtered regular code objects using `NAMESPACE`\nexports, it did not apply any filtering to S4 classes and methods.\n    *   Any S4 class that happened to be evaluated (because of assignment) was\nchecked, even if it was not exported. This led to false positives (reporting\nunexported S4 classes as undocumented).\n    *   Conversely, exported S4 classes\/methods defined without assignment were\nmissed entirely because they were never evaluated.\n\nIn contrast, `undoc(package=)` loads the installed package and checks the\nattached package environment, which naturally only contains exported S4 classes\nand methods.",
        "username": "r-bugs notifier",
        "icons": {
            "emoji": ":robot_face:"
        },
